// 51 pages, 8 sections with `.navigation.yml` and header sub-navigation, 198
// MDC blocks, 21 `routeRules` redirects, a landing page built from custom
// components), with Blume 2.1.3 (main). The agent read only the skill and the
// Blume docs it points to, and wrote one-off scripts for the MDC conversion.
// The old site was built with `nuxt generate` for its URL list and heading
// ids. Outcome, with `deployment: vercel()`: `blume build` passed (51 pages),
// `blume validate --strict` and `blume audit --only redirects` passed, all 72
// old URLs and all 50 `/raw/*.md` URLs were covered, and 34 heading ids were
// pinned. The build passed only after a workaround for the probe's symlinked
// Blume (Vercel's function-bundle check couldn't follow the symlinks); a real
// install wasn't tested. In `blume dev`, the MCP server answered `initialize`,
// `tools/list`, and a `search_docs` call, and the assistant route answered
// (no key was set, so no answer was generated).
// After the run: the bundled codemod (scripts/docus-codemod.mjs) was written
// from the run's scripts, then revised in review (code spans holding
// backticks, CRLF pages, multi-line HTML tags, `$$` math, blocks with slots it
// can't map, card descriptions, kebab-case props, `links` past `related`'s
// limit, case-sensitive tag names). The revised codemod, applied to a fresh
// copy of the same content, gave the same output as before: 82 callouts, 27
// cards, 27 fields, 25 code groups (4 to package-install), 18 prompts, 2 steps
// blocks, 247 fence labels, and the 8 `.navigation.yml` files converted, the
// prose hazards escaped, and the 7 install buttons and the landing page left
// for review; a second pass changed nothing. That output built with Blume (51
// pages), `blume validate --strict` reported only an anchor already dead on
// the old site, and pin-heading-ids.mjs paired 460 headings and found the same
// 34 to pin. On the run's `vercel()` project, the script with no `--dist` read
// dist/client by itself and paired the same 460. The codemod also converted
// the Docus docs (docus.dev, English; built once a malformed frontmatter key in
// the source was removed) and a second Docus 5 site, evloghq/evlog `apps/docs`
// at a2cfccadc23c8a85ab2165705c4b9a74cb724a9d (Docus ^5.13.0, 111 pages),
// which built with Blume once the one `related` list it flagged was trimmed; a
